IGS: preserve signed interface lookup errors before filling messages

Both NSS device lookup APIs return int32_t and use negative values on failure.
Keeping the result unsigned made both existing negative checks unreachable.
Preserve the existing bool failure contract and all normal message fields;
the driver send path's range guard remains an independent backstop.

--- a/nss_qdisc/igs/nss_ifb.c
+++ b/nss_qdisc/igs/nss_ifb.c
@@ -189,6 +189,6 @@ static bool nss_ifb_config_msg_fill(struct
 		int32_t ifb_num, enum nss_ifb_if_config config, void *cb)
 {
-	uint32_t if_src_num;
+	int32_t if_src_num;
 
 	if (netif_is_ifb_dev(dev)) {
 		if_src_num = nss_cmn_get_interface_number_by_dev_and_type(dev, NSS_DYNAMIC_INTERFACE_TYPE_IGS);
